                    {
                        "sense_id": "799ac52e-1994-33c9-8f5f-77a29fd54305",
                        "entry_id": "e115ae95-c2f9-3fab-b649-c8e1d420c8e4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Combat des Amazones contre les Athéniens."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Mythologie grecque"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1ffb9540-2437-35ce-8209-6a917f306852",
                        "entry_id": "e115ae95-c2f9-3fab-b649-c8e1d420c8e4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Thème iconographique de combat opposant des Amazones à des Grecs."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Mythologie grecque"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b1f2652-2a2d-476a-b50c-fc588bd87115",
                                "sense_id": "1ffb9540-2437-35ce-8209-6a917f306852",
                                "text": "Ciste ovale ornée d’une amazonomachie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68e0f7b8-417f-4255-a6dc-89f819c1d4f2",
                                "sense_id": "1ffb9540-2437-35ce-8209-6a917f306852",
                                "text": "L’autre point délicat est soulevé par les métopes du fronton ouest, dont les sculptures représentent nettement une amazonomachie."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2d5f71be-5496-48a6-9cfa-ffdbac2e0e85",
                        "source_entry_id": "e115ae95-c2f9-3fab-b649-c8e1d420c8e4",
                        "target_lang_word": "Amazonomachy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Amazonomachy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "78df2240-c63a-32f0-8fe2-96ab18c917e8",
                                        "entry_id": "5091c53e-e063-3aa1-bcd6-5b212a3f31b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of Amazonomachia (“a battle with Amazons (“mythical female warriors thought to inhabit the Black Sea region”); also (art), an artistic representation of such a scene”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5141524b-d685-492d-9c10-960aa40ff7f9",
                                                "sense_id": "78df2240-c63a-32f0-8fe2-96ab18c917e8",
                                                "text": "The usual themes are mythological, and of these certain ones enjoyed especial popularity. A few great mythical contests, viz., that of the Gods against the Giants, those of the Greeks against Centaurs, against Amazons, and against Trojans, supply subject matter to an impressively large number of decorative Greek sculptures. Of these themes the centauromachies and amazonomachies were the most often repeated."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35a7164f-1bf6-4ef8-813f-d02aa752bbe1",
                                                "sense_id": "78df2240-c63a-32f0-8fe2-96ab18c917e8",
                                                "text": "Several substantial fragments of a sarcophagus decorated with an Amazonomachy are in the possession of the Fogg Museum of Harvard University. […] The composition of the scene on the front is in three parts, the usual division of groups on sarcophagi with Amazonomachies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7759fe73-8954-4377-ad7d-104696d42cf6",
                                                "sense_id": "78df2240-c63a-32f0-8fe2-96ab18c917e8",
                                                "text": "Amazons exist in order to be fought, and ultimately defeated, by men in an Amazonomachy ('Amazon-battle'). […] Heracles' ninth labour was to fetch the girdle of the Amazon queen, Hippolyte, resulting in another Amazonomachy[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49845312-bcaf-457a-b3ca-8db835991c6b",
                                                "sense_id": "78df2240-c63a-32f0-8fe2-96ab18c917e8",
                                                "text": "One of the earliest studies of this frieze was by Schober, who drew attention to the 'north' section and its depiction of soldiers and Amazons: these are not engaged in battle as they would be in a regular Amazonomachy, but instead are enjoying cordial relations, shaking hands and clasping shoulders[…]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
